{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-327067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the two solutions to the equation $5\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}} and $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-327067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\sqrt{3} & =2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{3}{-\\sqrt{3}}=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\text{arctan}(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\pi +x=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}, \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\pi +x=2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are ${x}_{1}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-327067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6612beaf8e0032d1dc5cd7c9320856b8cdd9c8c6f14b2e8b6858738690f64225"} {"question" "q-327067" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-327067" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-327067" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-327067" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-326456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the two solutions to the equation $3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-326456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\sqrt{3} & =2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})={30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${30}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={30}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}={210}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x={30}^{∘}$ and $x={210}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-326456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6612beaf8e0032d1dc5cd7c9320856b8cdd9c8c6f14b2e8b6858738690f64225"} {"question" "q-326456" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-326456" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "30"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-326456" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-326456" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "210"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-274558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the two solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-\\sqrt{3}$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-274558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=-{30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince $-{30}^{∘}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={180}^{∘}+x={180}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}={150}^{∘}, \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\cdot {180}^{∘}+x=2\\cdot {180}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}={330}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x={150}^{∘}$ and $x={330}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-274558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6612beaf8e0032d1dc5cd7c9320856b8cdd9c8c6f14b2e8b6858738690f64225"} {"question" "q-274558" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-274558" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "150"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-274558" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-274558" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "330"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29207" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=1$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29207" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\text{arctan}(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{4}=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{4}=\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{16}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29207" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6612beaf8e0032d1dc5cd7c9320856b8cdd9c8c6f14b2e8b6858738690f64225"} {"question" "q-29207" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29207" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29207" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{16}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-120620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-120620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\text{arctan}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +x=\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{7\\pi }{6}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{6}=\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{36}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-120620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6612beaf8e0032d1dc5cd7c9320856b8cdd9c8c6f14b2e8b6858738690f64225"} {"question" "q-120620" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-120620" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{4{\\pi }^{2}}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}"] ["math" "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{36}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-120620" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{36}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation  $3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=20-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =20-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =20 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\text{arctan}(\\frac{1}{5})=(11.309\\,9…)^{∘}≈{11.310}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${11.310}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={11.310}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+{11.310}^{∘}={191.310}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is\n\n$$\n11.310\\cdot 191.310≈2\\,164\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6612beaf8e0032d1dc5cd7c9320856b8cdd9c8c6f14b2e8b6858738690f64225"} {"question" "q-29247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\,124"] ["math" "2\\,134"] ["math" "2\\,164"] ["math" "2\\,194"] ["math" "2\\,564"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\,164"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-327780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find, **in ascending order and rounded to the nearest integer**, the two solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{4}$  for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-327780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=4.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4)=(75.963\\,7…)^{∘}≈{75.964}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${75.964}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution, rounded to the nearest integer, is ${x}_{1}={76}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$\nHence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+x={180}^{∘}+{75.964}^{∘}≈{256}^{∘},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x={76}^{∘}$ and $x={256}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-327780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6612beaf8e0032d1dc5cd7c9320856b8cdd9c8c6f14b2e8b6858738690f64225"} {"question" "q-327780" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-327780" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "76"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-327780" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-327780" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "256"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29242" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation  $5\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=11+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29242" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =11+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =11 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =\\frac{11}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{4}{11}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\text{arctan}(\\frac{4}{11})=(19.983\\,1…)^{∘}≈{19.983}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${19.983}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={19.983}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+x={180}^{∘}+{19.983}^{∘}={199.983}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is\n\n$$\n19.983\\cdot 199.983≈3\\,996\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29242" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6612beaf8e0032d1dc5cd7c9320856b8cdd9c8c6f14b2