ademy/question-capture/13978897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6612beaf8e0032d1dc5cd7c9320856b8cdd9c8c6f14b2e8b6858738690f64225"} {"question" "q-327790" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-327790" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-327790" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-327790" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3.8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-330672" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find, **in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place**, the two solutions to the equation $2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-1=-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+13$ for $-\\pi <x<\\pi .$\n\n**In ascending order**, the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-330672" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-1 & =-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+13 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =14 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{7})=0.278\\,2…≈0.278\n$$\n\nSince $0.278$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution, rounded to one decimal place, is ${x}_{1}=0.3.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add and subtract integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-\\pi +x=-\\pi +0.278≈-2.9,\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place.\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-2.9$ and $x=0.3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-330672" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6612beaf8e0032d1dc5cd7c9320856b8cdd9c8c6f14b2e8b6858738690f64225"} {"question" "q-330672" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-330672" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2.9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-