teger multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=-\\pi +x=-\\pi +0.245\\,0=-2.896\\,6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=0.245\\,0,-2.896\\,6.$\n\nFinally, the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is \n\n$$\n0.245\\,0\\cdot (-2.896\\,6)≈-0.7\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6612beaf8e0032d1dc5cd7c9320856b8cdd9c8c6f14b2e8b6858738690f64225"} {"question" "q-29692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.6"] ["math" "-0.7"] ["math" "-0.8"] ["math" "-0.9"] ["math" "-1.2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-29692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-0.7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-330688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find, **in ascending order and rounded to the nearest integer**, the two solutions to the equation $4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+6$ for $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<{180}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-330688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+6 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =6 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})=(26.565\\,0…)^{∘}≈{26.565}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${26.565}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution, rounded to the nearest integer, is ${x}_{1}={27}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-{180}^{∘}+x=-{180}^{∘}+{26.565}^{∘}≈-{153}^{∘},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x={-153}^{∘}$ and $x={27}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-330688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6612beaf8e0032d1dc5cd7c9320856b8cdd9c8c6f14b2e8b6858738690f64225"} {"question" "q-330688" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-330688" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-153"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-330688" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-330688" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "27"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-120630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $4(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+1)=3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ for $-\\pi <x<\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to one decimal place?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-120630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+1) & =3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+4 & =3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{4})=-0.244\\,978≈-0.245\\,0\n$$\n\nSince $-0.245\\,0$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.245\\,0.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add and subtract integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=\\pi +x=\\pi -0.245\\,0≈2.896\\,6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-0.245\\,0,2.896\\,6.$\n\nFinally, the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is \n\n$$\n(-0.245\\,0)\\cdot 2.896\\,6≈-0.7\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-120630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6612beaf8e0032d1dc5cd7c9320856b8cdd9c8c6f14b2e8b6858738690f64225"} {"question" "q-120630" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c754dc690a836b9ca4b87b9b05ffe34a8684e62be8a66d213448616d0770ad7"} {"question" "q-120630" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.5"] ["math" "-0.7"] ["math" "-1.2"] ["math" "-1.8"] ["math" "-2.1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978897/state.json" "file_sha